{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "12", "m": "11", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "43", "S": "25"}}, "news": [{"title": "Somany Ceramics plans 16 million sq metre glazed vitrified tiles capacity addition", "para": "Somany Ceramics is set to expand its capacity for glazed vitrified tiles significantly within the next 18 months. By enhancing its joint venture in South India, the company expects to double output at this facility. Plans also include increasing production by adding four million square meters through debottlenecking existing plants.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/somany-ceramics-plans-16-million-sq-metre-glazed-vitrified-tiles-capacity-addition/135755179?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-1611255/135755179.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "FIRs issued against two Greater Bengaluru authority officials for issuing illegal e-khatas", "para": "Two assistant commissioners from the Greater Bengaluru Authority were suspended for issuing fraudulent e-khatas. They allegedly colluded with builders to misuse the e-Aasthi system's SARFAESI module. Officials approved applications using unrelated documents instead of mandatory SARFAESI orders. As a result, investigations were initiated for serious misconduct and abuse of official position. The case highlights significant violations under the Greater Bengaluru Governance Act.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/firs-issued-against-two-greater-bengaluru-authority-officials-for-issuing-illegal-e-khatas/135755127?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-43284/135755127.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Three Udyog Vihar construction sites among five sealed over dust violations in Gurugram", "para": "Five construction sites in Gurgaon were sealed for failing to comply with dust-control regulations during an inspection. The Haryana State Pollution Control Board conducted enforcement actions against sites for violations of air quality management directions. Construction sites are required to adhere to prescribed dust-mitigation measures to prevent dust emissions. Inspections will continue across the region as authorities seek to improve compliance.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/three-udyog-vihar-construction-sites-among-five-sealed-over-dust-violations-in-gurugram/135755031?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-243228/135755031.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}